  "releaseNotes": "## What's Changed\n\n### Features\n- **Add .NET 11 support with runtime-async** (#190) — Multi-targets . Enables  for  across all libraries and benchmarks.\n\n### Performance\n- **Dedicated single-entity attribute fetch with early exit** (#189) — New  on  returns  instead of . Breaks inner loop after first match per attribute name, eliminating the O(n) full-bucket scan. : 127 µs → 6.5 µs (~20x speedup), allocs 3983 B → 3467 B.\n- **Reduce GC pressure in function check hot path** (#188) —  changed from heap-allocated  to , eliminating one allocation per lambda invocation. Remove intermediate  in  by indexing directly into args array. Pre-compute  at construction time on . Replace  in hot paths with . Gen0: 15.6 → 8.8 per 1000 ops (~44% reduction).\n- **DataTable TVPs to SqlDataRecord** (#168) by @makeentosch — Replaces -based TVP construction with , reducing allocations in SqlServer write paths.\n\n### Bug Fixes\n- **Schema-keyed SQL cache and pure snap token resolution** (#185, #184) by @jafin — SQL query cache now keyed by schema so multi-schema deployments don't share cached queries across schemas. Snap token resolution made pure (no side effects). Covers both Postgres and SqlServer.\n- **Qualify  type name with configured schema** (#182) by @jafin — SqlServer TVP type lookup now respects the configured DB schema instead of defaulting to .\n- **Allow permission bodies to reference themselves and forward-declare other permissions** (#180) by @jafin — Lang parser now handles self-referential and forward-referenced permission bodies without error.\n- **Don't cancel memoized tasks via short-circuit CTS in CheckEngine** (#177) — Fixes a race where the short-circuit  would cancel in-flight memoized tasks still needed by other branches.\n\n### CI / Infrastructure\n- Replace SonarCloud with independent coverage collection\n- Coveralls integration with per-PR changed-file coverage\n- Coverage collected on push to \n- Drop Cake build script — version and release notes now managed outside source\n- Benchmark workflow fixes (base benchmarks, PR comment posting, concurrency cancellation)\n- Bump  → 5.3.0,  → 21,  → 3\n\n## New Contributors\n- @makeentosch made their first contribution in #168\n- @jafin made their first contribution in #180",
